  "shorterRoute": "Reuse the all-word original rank-two theorem and the surjective integral cusp presentation; no second determinant descent or free rank proof is needed. Native finite-product tensor base change retains literal coordinates. The already proved original p-adic eigencharacter supplies compatibility on every integral operator, and existing prime generation extends scalar action. The existing algebraIdempotentLeftIdeal and native range/submodule equivalences identify the normalized character image with the prescribed two coefficient coordinates. The same arithmetic projector is used for rank two and restricted Weil nondegeneracy. A direct large-expression rewrite was replaced by a finite-algebra surjective-descent lemma at unchanged proof limits. The alternative full tensor-associativity reconstruction and a new eigencharacter construction were assessed and deferred because the existing character and all-word coordinates suffice.",
  "assumptionsToDischarge": "The transported arithmetic projector has a nonzero rank-two image on the actual original coefficient-extended Tate module, and its literal root-valued Weil pairing is injective on that same image. Generator, integral-character compatibility, action comparison and dimension hypotheses are all derived from the original upstream objects.",
  "remaining": "The image coordinate equivalence still needs comparison with the existing spanning primitive specialization. The cyclotomic law must yield the separate primitive Frobenius determinant; the quadratic identity alone is insufficient. Residual association, arithmetic automorphy and all-weight continuation remain required. 16/20; DUB-17--20 OPEN.",
